Thanks for the clear answers.

Here is snippet of my `infobox`, I am not sure it is the right way but it does work, if it can help someone.

```js
<!-- require infobox.js -->

var search = instantsearch({
  appId: xxx,
  apiKey: xxx,
  indexName: xxx
});

var o = new InfoBox({/*options*/});

var map = instantsearch.widgets.geoSearch({
  container: '#map',
  googleReference: window.google,
  customHTMLMarker: {
    template:  function(e) {
      return '<div>' + e.title + '</div>'
    },
    events: {
      click: function(e) {
        o.getMap() && o.close(), o.setContent('<div>' + e.item.title + '</div>'), o.open(e.map, e.marker)
      }
    }
  },
});

search.addWidget(map);
search.start();
```

**Question about Places with GeoSearch:**
I am now trying to display an *Algolia Places* [search input](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/v2/dev-novel/?selectedStory=GeoSearch.with%20position%20from%20Places) to my `geoSearch` widget. I gathered that the *Places* script is already included in `instantsearch.js`, so I don't need to reference it.

But I am having hard times to understand how to implement it, could someone give me a simple example?

*It could be nice if the [examples](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/v2/dev-novel) had a little snippet to copy.*
